35,2,1,talk,Midori,,The shared clinic failed because no one owned the rota. That is a warning.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The call-back trial worked, but only while it was funded. It stopped, and results slipped.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"Therapy staff are leaving, but midwifery has slack. That imbalance is key.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shion,,The budget is down a quarter. And data agreements take fourteen months. That kills external links.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shizue,,The rooms are full by mid-morning. The booking system only tracks fixed slots.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, the data agreement delay is a major hurdle for any external coordination.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,Yes. And the therapy unit is losing people. A new rehab unit might struggle to staff.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Misaki,,Midwifery has capacity. That suggests a perinatal focus might be feasible without new hires.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shion,,"If we can't afford the fit-out, and can't link data, we are limited to internal, low-tech solutions.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"If it doesn't fit in the booking system, it doesn't exist. We need something that uses existing slots.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Midori,,Home visits are hard to track in the current system. That is a risk.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,The readmission drop was real. But it required active follow-up.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Misaki,,A perinatal service could use the midwifery slack. It fits the staffing reality.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shion,,"It is cheap to start. No new rooms, no external data links. Just time.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shizue,,It can be scheduled as fixed slots. The booking system can handle it.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Midori,,I am leaning towards the perinatal option. It avoids the staffing and data traps.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"It is a quiet, sustainable choice. I agree.","{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Misaki,,The staffing data supports it. I support it.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shion,,It is the only one that fits the budget and the system constraints.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shizue,,It fits the rooms and the schedule. I am comfortable with this.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
